# AutoClaw relay channel credential, classified by service.
#
# Install as /etc/facai-cloud/providers/relay.env, owned by root:facai with
# mode 0640:
#   install -d -m 0750 -o root -g facai /etc/facai-cloud/providers
#   install -m 0640 -o root -g facai relay.env.example /etc/facai-cloud/providers/relay.env
# Then edit it and fill in the real value. NEVER commit this file with values.
#
# Facai reads these by name from the process environment and never prints or
# returns their values. Until the secret is present the channel reports
# UNCONFIGURED: the webhook refuses with 503 and the outbox stays empty.
#
# RISK NOTE: AutoClaw drives a PERSONAL WhatsApp account through unofficial
# means. That risk is the operator's own choice; Facai Cloud never contacts
# WhatsApp and only receives AutoClaw's HTTP forwarding.
#
# Shared secret used as the HMAC-SHA256 key for both directions, exactly like
# the n8n integration: X-Facai-Signature: sha256=<hex> over "<timestamp>.<body>"
# with X-Facai-Timestamp. Use a long random value; the same value is configured
# in the AutoClaw bridge client.
RELAY_SHARED_SECRET=
# Optional tuning. Leave empty to use the default shown.
# RELAY_MAX_SKEW=300
